=========================================================================
FINDINGS (backlog; none of them is a criterion failure)
=========================================================================
F1 (attributed to CM1, brief's exclusion premise disproven).
   The brief says "If a test run leaves testdata/settings/whatif.json modified,
   that is a pre-existing suite defect (report it, do not FAIL on it)". It is NOT
   pre-existing. Controlled experiment, same tree, same command:
     - CM1 state:  go test -count=1 ./cmd/server -> ok; then
       cmp master-content vs testdata/settings/whatif.json ->
       "differ: byte 131, line 6"; diff adds "use_current_month": true and
       moves "start_date": "2026-04" -> "2026-09".
     - Same tree with the CM1 change reverted (git checkout master -- <6 source
       files>, rm the 5 new test files), same `go test -count=1 ./cmd/server`
       -> ok, and cmp -> IDENTICAL (control leaves fixture untouched).
     - Independently: full `go test -count=1 ./...` on a pristine `git archive
       master` export -> exit 0, fixture IDENTICAL; full `go test -count=1 ./...`
       on the CM1 tree -> exit 0, fixture MODIFIED.
   Cause: cmd/server tests use the repo-tracked testdata/ as their data dir, and
   the new migration persists on first load. Consequence: the pre-commit
   `make check` (which runs `go test ./...`) now dirties a tracked fixture whose
   content is time-dependent (start_date = the month the suite last ran). The
   oracle's step 4 cannot see this because it only runs the zzoracle package and
   the -run CurrentMonth subset, never ./cmd/server. I am reporting, not failing,
   per the brief's explicit instruction; the lead may want to revisit given the
   premise is false.
F2 Mutation F (new-plan default `settings.UseCurrentMonth = true` ->
   `= false` in loadInternalContext's missing-file branch) SURVIVES: the full
   retirement + whatif packages stay green AND accept.sh still prints
   ORACLE PASS. The "default true for new plans" half of criterion C1 is
   correct in the delivered code (proven by my probe) but has no permanent
   guard. V3-pattern promotion candidate: my probe asserts
   Load()-on-empty-dir => UseCurrentMonth==true and the first Save persists
   use_current_month:true / start_date==now.
F3 Mutation H (drop `resolveCurrentMonth` from saveInternal) is caught ONLY by
   the transient oracle; the permanent suite stays green (the load-side
   resolution masks it on every read-back). Once the oracle directory is
   retired, "on save, StartDate resolves" has no regression guard. Promotion
   candidate: assert the on-disk start_date after Save of a stale settings
   object.
F4 (pre-existing on master, backlog only) `gofmt -l internal cmd` reports 22
   unformatted files on master (e.g. internal/handlers/accounts/handlers.go,
   internal/services/mcpsvc/plan/register.go). None is a CM1 file; `make check`
   does not run gofmt, so this is invisible to the pipeline.
